Fix: when the very first DESCRIBE for the video subsession races the
capture source's first frame (e.g. right after v4l2rtspserver starts,
before camd's SPS/PPS have been read even once), wait briefly (bounded,
3s max) for H264_V4L2DeviceSource::getAuxLine() to become non-empty
before building the SDP. Once built, this SDP line is cached for the
process's whole lifetime (OnDemandServerMediaSubsession::fSDPLines), so
without this a premature empty result here permanently starves RTSP
clients of sprop-parameter-sets until the next process restart.

Root-caused via `this`-pointer tracing on real hardware: confirmed the
same H264_V4L2DeviceSource object backs both the capture thread
(splitFrames(), which does detect SPS/PPS reliably) and this DESCRIBE
handler -- it's a genuine startup race, not a stale/wrong source
instance. See docs/20260813_video信頼性_sprop捕捉機構特定_技術相談.md.

--- a/src/ServerMediaSubsession.cpp
+++ b/src/ServerMediaSubsession.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 ** -------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
 #include <sstream>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <linux/videodev2.h>
 
 // project
@@ -119,6 +120,27 @@
 			os << rtpSink->auxSDPLine();
 		}
 		else if (source) {
+			/* atomcam2: the very first DESCRIBE for this subsession can race
+			 * the capture source's first frame -- e.g. right after
+			 * v4l2rtspserver starts, before the encoder's SPS/PPS have been
+			 * read even once. Once this SDP line is built it is cached for
+			 * the process's whole lifetime
+			 * (OnDemandServerMediaSubsession::fSDPLines), so a premature
+			 * empty result here means RTSP clients never see
+			 * sprop-parameter-sets until the next restart. Wait briefly
+			 * (bounded) for the capture thread to produce it before giving
+			 * up -- confirmed via `this`-pointer tracing that this is a
+			 * genuine same-object startup race, not a stale/wrong source
+			 * (see docs/20260813_video信頼性_sprop捕捉機構特定_技術相談.md). */
+			if (source->getAuxLine().empty()) {
+				int waited_ms = 0;
+				while (source->getAuxLine().empty() && waited_ms < 3000) {
+					usleep(100 * 1000);
+					waited_ms += 100;
+				}
+				LOG(NOTICE) << "getAuxLine: waited " << waited_ms << "ms for capture source; sprop "
+					<< (source->getAuxLine().empty() ? "still empty" : "ready");
+			}
 			unsigned char rtpPayloadType = rtpSink->rtpPayloadType();
 			DeviceInterface* device = source->getDevice();
 			os << "a=fmtp:" << int(rtpPayloadType) << " " << source->getAuxLine() << "\r\n";				
